            The best paleo protein powder for most people is the least glamorous one: plain egg white. It is complete, carries close to a whey-level dose of leucine per scoop, contains no bone, and costs less per gram than the beef and bone broth powders that dominate paleo marketing. Naked Egg is our pick, with NOW Sports as the budget alternative.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If eggs are off the table, choose a beef isolate and take two scoops, Transparent Labs for a flavored shake or Equip Unflavored for a strict single-ingredient label. Keep bone broth and collagen for what they do well, adding protein and glycine to coffee, soups and meals, and do not pay bone broth prices for your main muscle-building shake.
